  "source": {
    "citation": "Zi-Xiao Huang, From Weyl Anomaly to Universal Defect Casimir Energy and Rényi Entropy, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/fz81-ysss",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/fz81-ysss",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2501.09498v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper derives closed-form expressions for the contribution of surface defects to supersymmetric Rényi entropy and Casimir energy in 6d (2,0) theories, expressed in terms of defect Weyl anomaly coefficients b and d2. The main result is the defect SRE formula S_gamma = (2b - d2)/6 * [r1 r2/2 (gamma - 1) + 1] log(ell/epsilon), with explicit b and d2 for symmetric and antisymmetric representations of A_(N-1). The paper also covers holographic large-N checks, localization results, and anomaly polynomial derivations.",
