    {
      "mechanism_id": "defect_sre_formula",
      "statement": "The defect contribution to supersymmetric Rényi entropy for 1/2-BPS Wilson surfaces in 6d A_(N-1) (2,0) theories is a linear function of gamma=1/n, given by S_gamma = (2b - d2)/6 * [r1 r2/2 (gamma - 1) + 1] log(ell/epsilon), where b and d2 are the defect Weyl anomaly coefficients.",
